# nghttp2 -- HTTP/2 for libsoup3, which takes dependency('libnghttp2') with no
# option guard.
#
# Here for gnome-software. Also relevant to ostree, whose --disable-http2 was
# set because Duct's curl is built without nghttp2 -- so once this lands, curl
# and ostree both become revisitable. That is recorded in ostree's pkg.env as a
# thing to revisit rather than left for someone to rediscover.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://github.com/nghttp2/nghttp2/releases/download/v1.66.0/nghttp2-1.66.0.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=00ba1bdf0ba2c74b2a4fe6c8b1069dc9d82f82608af24442d430df97c6f9e631
SRC_DIR=nghttp2-1.66.0

# --enable-lib-only IS THE WHOLE RECIPE, and it is the cleanest option upstream
# has offered all week: it builds libnghttp2 and nothing else.
#
# Without it, configure probes for the pieces of an entire HTTP/2 SERVER AND
# PROXY -- nghttp, nghttpd and nghttpx -- along with hpack-tools and examples,
# both of which default to 'check'. Those want libev, libc-ares, jansson,
# libevent and a C++ compiler, and what they cannot find they silently omit. So
# the alternative to this one flag is a package whose contents depend on which
# unrelated libraries happen to be in the seed.
#
# libsoup needs the library. Nothing in this distribution needs an HTTP/2 proxy.
#
# AND THERE IS A SECOND REASON THIS FLAG EARNS ITS PLACE, which only became
# visible after sweeping libarchive: --enable-lib-only does not merely shrink
# the OUTPUT, it removes the PROBING SURFACE. The applications it declines to
# build are the things that would have link-probed libev, c-ares, jansson and
# libevent -- so there is no set of auto-detected dependencies to enumerate,
# reason about, or fail to declare.
#
# libarchive is the contrast: it probes twenty-four libraries with no way to
# turn the probing off, so its recipe has to account for every one and its
# dependency list has to be maintained against the seed. Here there is nothing
# to account for.
# AN OPTION THAT SHRINKS THE PROBE SURFACE IS WORTH MORE THAN ONE THAT SHRINKS
# THE OUTPUT, because the second saves disk and the first removes a category of
# undeclared dependency.
#
# --disable-examples and --disable-hpack-tools are therefore redundant with
# --enable-lib-only and are NOT passed; the value is recorded here instead, for
# the same reason as xdg-dbus-proxy's installed_tests.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static --enable-lib-only"
